{"id":"cluster-administration-proxies","corpus":"k8s","title":"Proxies in Kubernetes","sourceUrl":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/cluster-administration/proxies/","license":"Kubernetes Documentation © The Kubernetes Authors, licensed CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Proxies in Kubernetes"},{"kind":"p","text":"This page explains proxies used with Kubernetes."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Proxies"},{"kind":"p","text":"There are several different proxies you may encounter when using Kubernetes:"},{"kind":"li","text":"The kubectl proxy:"},{"kind":"li","text":"runs on a user's desktop or in a pod"},{"kind":"li","text":"proxies from a localhost address to the Kubernetes apiserver"},{"kind":"li","text":"client to proxy uses HTTP"},{"kind":"li","text":"proxy to apiserver uses HTTPS"},{"kind":"li","text":"locates apiserver"},{"kind":"li","text":"adds authentication headers"},{"kind":"li","text":"The apiserver proxy:"},{"kind":"li","text":"is a bastion built into the apiserver"},{"kind":"li","text":"connects a user outside of the cluster to cluster IPs which otherwise might not be reachable"},{"kind":"li","text":"runs in the apiserver processes"},{"kind":"li","text":"client to proxy uses HTTPS (or http if apiserver so configured)"},{"kind":"li","text":"proxy to target may use HTTP or HTTPS as chosen by proxy using available information"},{"kind":"li","text":"can be used to reach a Node, Pod, or Service"},{"kind":"li","text":"does load balancing when used to reach a Service"},{"kind":"li","text":"The kube proxy:"},{"kind":"li","text":"runs on each node"},{"kind":"li","text":"proxies UDP, TCP and SCTP"},{"kind":"li","text":"does not understand HTTP"},{"kind":"li","text":"provides load balancing"},{"kind":"li","text":"is only used to reach services"},{"kind":"li","text":"A Proxy/Load-balancer in front of apiserver(s):"},{"kind":"li","text":"existence and implementation varies from cluster to cluster (e.g. nginx)"},{"kind":"li","text":"sits between all clients and one or more apiservers"},{"kind":"li","text":"acts as load balancer if there are several apiservers."},{"kind":"li","text":"Cloud Load Balancers on external services:"},{"kind":"li","text":"are provided by some cloud providers (e.g. AWS ELB, Google Cloud Load Balancer)"},{"kind":"li","text":"are created automatically when the Kubernetes service has type LoadBalancer"},{"kind":"li","text":"usually supports UDP/TCP only"},{"kind":"li","text":"SCTP support is up to the load balancer implementation of the cloud provider"},{"kind":"li","text":"implementation varies by cloud provider."},{"kind":"p","text":"Kubernetes users will typically not need to worry about anything other than the first two types. The cluster admin will typically ensure that the latter types are set up correctly."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Requesting redirects"},{"kind":"p","text":"Proxies have replaced redirect capabilities. Redirects have been deprecated."}],"lemmas":{"proxies":["proxy","proxies"],"kubernetes":["kubernetes","kubernete"],"pages":["page","pages"],"paging":["paging","page"],"explains":["explains","explain"],"explained":["explained","explain"],"explaining":["explaining","explain"],"used":["used","use"],"useds":["useds","used"],"severals":["severals","several"],"differents":["differents","different"],"mays":["may","mays"],"might":["might","may"],"encounters":["encounter","encounters"],"encountered":["encountered","encounter"],"encountering":["encountering","encounter"],"whens":["whens","when"],"using":["using","use"],"usings":["using","usings"],"kubectls":["kubectls","kubectl"],"runs":["run","runs"],"running":["running","run"],"ran":["ran","run"],"user's":["user"],"desktops":["desktop","desktops"],"pods":["pod","pods"],"localhosts":["localhosts","localhost"],"addresses":["address","addresses"],"addressing":["addressing","address"],"addressed":["addressed","address"],"uses":["use","uses"],"locates":["locates","locate"],"located":["located","